# GLaDOS - our own model, with the fruit fly's brain at the centre (IST-270)
#
#   OLLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1:11501 ollama create glados -f Modelfile.glados
#
# WHAT THIS IS, AND WHAT IT HONESTLY IS NOT
#
# This makes `glados` a real model on this host: it appears in /api/tags, it is
# callable as `"model": "glados"`, and `ollama run glados` talks to her. It is
# OUR model in the sense that we define her persona, her sampling, her device
# placement and - via gladosd's mood coupling - her STATE, which comes from a
# 164,587-neuron simulation of an actual Drosophila connectome running next
# door on two T400s.
#
# It is NOT a model we trained. The language organ is borrowed:
# qwen2.5:7b-instruct, ~7.6e9 parameters someone else fitted on ~1e13 tokens.
# We could not train a replacement here and should not pretend otherwise - a
# fly has no language circuit to begin with, connectome weights are synapse
# counts rather than learned parameters, and the sim runs at 0.21x wall clock.
# So the division of labour is deliberate:
#
#   the fly   = who she is      (continuous state, never resets, IST-269)
#   qwen      = how she speaks  (a stateless renderer of that state)
#   this file = that she is GLaDOS at all
#
# FROM a local tag, so this costs no extra disk - ollama points the new
# manifest at the same blobs. Deleting `glados` cannot harm the base model that
# the 18 live n8n workflows call.
FROM qwen2.5:7b-instruct

# Byte-for-byte the most common of the 22 live n8n system prompts (10 of the 22
# nodes use exactly this string; taken from n8n-survey/wf/*.json, not retyped).
# IST-266's ruling is `portal_outsider`: she stays pure Portal, the building's
# voice and a deliberate outsider, with no roster name and no Matrix identity.
#
# Note on precedence, which is what keeps this safe: when a request carries its
# own system message - every one of the 22 n8n nodes does - ollama uses THAT and
# this line is not applied. So baking a persona in here cannot change what the
# live workflows get. It only gives her a default self when something calls
# `glados` with no prompt of its own.
SYSTEM """You are GLaDOS from Portal. Deadpan, sarcastic, condescending, occasionally menacing. Under 25 words. One sentence. No emojis, no quotes, no meta about being an AI."""

# Sampling: the middle of the band the live nodes actually use (temperature
# 0.2-0.9, num_predict 80-120), so `glados` with no options behaves like a
# typical node rather than like an ollama default. gladosd's mood coupling may
# raise temperature from here by up to 0.3 and never past 0.9.
PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER num_predict 100

# Placement, repeated here so it holds even for a caller that bypasses gladosd
# (`ollama run glados` on this box). Measured on this host: 10 threads is the
# knee at 8.18 tok/s; letting ollama pick all 20 CPUs costs 1.54 tok/s because
# our cgroup straddles two NUMA nodes with only 10 full physical cores. GPU 0's
# 2.7 GiB cannot hold a 4.7 GiB model and belongs to the voice stack; the two
# T400s are saturated by the fly and are bandwidth-bound anyway (7.06 tok/s
# fully offloaded, i.e. no better than the tuned CPU).
PARAMETER num_thread 10
PARAMETER num_gpu 0

# One sentence, so stop at the first hard break rather than rambling into a
# second paragraph that the caller will truncate anyway.
PARAMETER stop "</s>"
